|desc=A horrible phantasm rises to stand before enemy creatures in the area of effect, causing them to make a will [[saving throw|save]]. If they fail, the phantasm touches them and they must now make a fortitude saving throw. If this saving throw fails, the creature dies. Those who succeed the fortitude save still take 3[[d6]] points of [[magical damage]]. Creatures with less than 4 [[hit dice]] automatically die, without any saving throws.}}

== Notes ==

* The mind-affecting descriptor applies to the "versus" part of the will saving throw. The fortitude save is versus death even though this is not [[death magic]] (immunity to death magic does not apply).
* Immunity to the descriptors (fear or mind-affecting) is applied before the saving throws (if any) and after the spell resistance check, with no feedback if this immunity applies.
* Due to a .2da bug, ''true seeing'' is not an additional [[counterspell]] of this spell.

=== Previous versions ===

* Prior to version 1.66, immunity to death magic did prevent death from this spell.
* Prior to version 1.66, the mind-affecting immunity from ''[[protection from evil]]'' was ignored.

